    <bpmn:process id="W_W1173" name="W1173. High-Risk SKU Protection Plan &amp; Product Security Fixture Deployment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual shrinkage analysis identifies high-theft categories; or new high-value product category launch; or store remodel/refresh
Frequency: Annual plan review; quarterly deployment execution; ad-hoc for new categories
Volume: ~1,500–2,000 high-risk SKUs across chain (out of 35,000 active); ~200 stores requiring security fixture maintenance
Owner: LP Manager (Regional)
Participants: LP Analyst, Category Manager, Store Manager, LP Training Coordinator, Security Equipment Vendor
Source: workflow W1173 — High-Risk SKU Protection Plan &amp; Product Security Fixture Deployment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1173_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1173_Lane1" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1173_Lane2" name="LP Manager + Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1173_Lane3" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1173_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1173_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1173_Start6" name="Annual shrinkage analysis identifies high-theft categories; or new high-value product…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1173_Task7" name="High-risk SKU identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: High-risk SKU identification: Annual shrinkage analysis per W845 identifies top-theft SKUs by: (a) shrinkage value (quantity × cost), (b) shrinkage rate (shrinkage quantity ÷ sales quantity), (c) theft pattern (external shoplifting vs. internal employee theft); LP Analyst classifies SKUs into protection tiers: Tier A (locked case, behind counter): items &gt; PHP 10,000 or top-50 shrinkage value; Tier B (Spider Wrap / Alpha Keeper): items PHP 2,000–10,000 with high shrinkage rate; Tier C (EAS tag + shelf positioning): items &lt; PHP 2,000 with moderate shrinkage
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1173_Task8" name="Protection plan per category">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Protection plan per category: For each Tier A/B category, LP Manager designs protection plan with Category Manager: (a) power tools: locked glass display case with sample tools on display; full inventory behind counter; customer requests specific model, staff retrieves from secure storage; (b) electrical fittings: Spider Wrap on multi-packs; individual fittings in Alpha Keepers; high-value breakers in locked peg hook area; (c) plumbing fittings (brass/copper): secured bin display with employee-access-only backing; (d) adhesives/sealants: EAS tag + shelf positioning near high-traffic aisle; (e) Category Manager approves plan ensuring sales conversion impact is acceptable
Responsible (R): LP Manager (Regional) + Category Manager
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1 day/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1173_Task9" name="Fixture procurement &amp; deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fixture procurement &amp; deployment: For new security fixtures: (a) LP Manager orders locked display cases, Spider Wraps, Alpha Keepers, secured peg hooks from security equipment vendor; (b) schedule installation during store remodel or low-traffic period; (c) Store Manager coordinates installation with vendor; (d) train staff on fixture access procedures (key management, Spider Wrap removal at POS); (e) system updates high-risk SKU protection tier assignment for POS deactivation procedures
Responsible (R): LP Manager / Store Manager / Vendor
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1–2 weeks/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1173_Task10" name="POS integration for security deactivation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: POS integration for security deactivation: System ensures: (a) Tier A items: POS requires manager key swipe to authorize sale; (b) Tier B items: POS prompts cashier to remove Spider Wrap/Alpha Keeper and scan deactivation barcode; (c) all high-risk items: POS enforces quantity threshold alert — if customer purchases &gt; 3 units of a Tier A item, alert LP Analyst for potential ORC per W840
Responsible (R): System / IT
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: Per IT sprint</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1173_Task11" name="Quarterly compliance verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly compliance verification: LP Analyst conducts quarterly store visit to verify: (a) security fixtures intact and functional, (b) high-risk SKUs correctly placed in designated protection fixtures, (c) Spider Wraps/Alpha Keepers applied to all Tier B items, (d) EAS tags present on all Tier C items, (e) locked case keys secured and access logged; compliance score feeds store LP scorecard
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager (Regional)
Duration: 60 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1173_Task12" name="Annual plan refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual plan refresh: LP Manager reviews annual shrinkage data vs. protection plan: (a) did protected categories show shrinkage reduction? (b) are new categories emerging as high-theft? (c) should any categories be re-tiered? (d) fixture maintenance/replacement needs; update plan for next fiscal year
Responsible (R): LP Manager (Regional)
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1173_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1173_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1173_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1173_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-312 (ensure controlled execution — Shrinkage Reduction (PA-23.3).) | - operational: LP Manager (Regional) review and approval gate
Owner: LP Manager (Regional)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1173_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1173_Annotation14" targetRef="W1173_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
