    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1174" name="W1174. Loss Prevention Store Compliance Audit Program &amp; Scoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly per store; or triggered by shrinkage result spike, exception report anomaly (W837), or anonymous tip
Frequency: Monthly per store (200 stores = ~200 audits/month); within the monthly cadence each store receives ~1 comprehensive and ~2 spot-check audits per quarter
Volume: ~200 audits/month per the Frequency (comprehensive + spot-check variants); ~2,400 audits/year
Owner: LP Auditor
Participants: LP Auditor, Store Manager, Department Supervisor, LP Manager (Regional), National LP Director
Source: workflow W1174 — Loss Prevention Store Compliance Audit Program &amp; Scoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1174_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1174_Lane1" name="LP Auditor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1174_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1174_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1174_Lane4" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1174_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1174_Start6" name="Scheduled — monthly per store; or triggered by shrinkage result spike, exception report…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1174_Task7" name="Audit schedule &amp; preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Audit schedule &amp; preparation: LP Auditor receives monthly audit schedule from LP Manager (Regional); each auditor covers ~40–50 stores; for comprehensive audits: pre-load audit checklist on tablet with store-specific data: current shrinkage rate, exception report trends per W837, previous audit findings and remediation status, high-risk SKU list per W1173
Responsible (R): LP Auditor
Accountable (A): LP Manager (Regional)
Duration: 30 min/store prep</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1174_Task8" name="Comprehensive audit execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Comprehensive audit execution (quarterly per store): LP Auditor conducts in-store assessment covering 10 LP domains: (a) Cash handling: cash drawer procedures, safe access log, deposit preparation, dual-control compliance; (b) Receiving: DSD verification per W1168, goods receipt accuracy, dock door security; (c) EAS compliance: tag application rate per W844, deactivator functionality, gate alarm response; (d) High-risk SKU protection: fixture integrity per W1173, correct tiering, key management; (e) Refund/return controls: authorization compliance, ID verification, receipt validation per W841; (f) CCTV &amp; access control: camera uptime per W838, recording integrity, restricted area access; (g) Backroom security: receiving dock access, stock room access, trash compactor area (concealment point); (h) LP awareness: staff knowledge of reporting procedures, whistleblower channel, LP policy; (i) Vendor compliance: vendor ID verification, delivery appointment adherence, dock security per W843; (j) Documentation: LP log maintenance, incident reporting accuracy, corrective action closure
Responsible (R): LP Auditor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1174_Task9" name="Spot-check audit execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Spot-check audit execution (alternate quarters): Focused 60-min audit targeting 1–2 domains based on: (a) previous comprehensive audit deficiencies, (b) current shrinkage trend, (c) exception report alerts per W837; faster format allows more frequent store visits without disrupting operations
Responsible (R): LP Auditor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1174_Task10" name="Scoring &amp; rating">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Scoring &amp; rating: System scores each domain on 1–5 scale: 1 = Non-compliant (critical gap), 2 = Below standard, 3 = Partially compliant, 4 = Compliant, 5 = Best practice; overall store score calculated as weighted average: cash handling (20%), receiving (15%), EAS (15%), high-risk SKU (15%), refund controls (10%), CCTV (5%), backroom (5%), LP awareness (5%), vendor compliance (5%), documentation (5%); overall rating: A (≥ 4.5), B (3.5–4.4), C (2.5–3.4), D (&lt; 2.5 — requires immediate action plan)
Responsible (R): System / LP Auditor
Accountable (A): LP Manager (Regional)
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1174_Task11" name="Findings debrief">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Findings debrief: LP Auditor debriefs Store Manager on findings: (a) review each domain score with specific observations, (b) highlight critical findings requiring immediate remediation, (c) acknowledge areas of excellence, (d) agree on remediation actions with deadlines, (e) Store Manager signs acknowledgment
Responsible (R): LP Auditor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1174_Task12" name="Remediation tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Remediation tracking: Store Manager executes corrective actions; system tracks remediation progress with deadlines; LP Auditor follows up on critical findings within 30 days; unresolved critical findings escalated to Regional Manager; repeated D ratings escalated to VP Store Operations with potential Store Manager performance action
Responsible (R): Store Manager / LP Auditor
Accountable (A): LP Manager (Regional)
Duration: 30 min/follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1174_Task13" name="Monthly reporting &amp; analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly reporting &amp; analytics: LP Manager (Regional) compiles monthly audit analytics: (a) average store score by region, (b) most common deficiencies, (c) remediation closure rate, (d) score trend by store, (e) correlation between audit score and shrinkage rate; present to National LP Director for strategic decisions
Responsible (R): LP Manager (Regional)
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1174_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1174_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1174_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1174_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-312 (ensure controlled execution — Shrinkage Reduction (PA-23.3).) | - operational: LP Auditor review and approval gate
Owner: LP Auditor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1174_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1174_Annotation15" targetRef="W1174_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
