    <bpmn:process id="W_W1249" name="W1249. Consignment &amp; Vendor-Managed Inventory Shrinkage Monitoring &amp; Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly consignment reconciliation cycle; ad-hoc triggered by consignment sell-through variance, VMI replenishment discrepancy, or vendor audit finding
Frequency: Monthly reconciliation per vendor; quarterly deep-dive for all consignment/VMI partners
Volume: ~12 VMI vendors (300 SKUs); ~25 consignment vendors (appliances, tiles); ~37 monthly reconciliations
Owner: LP Analyst / Inventory Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Vendor Account Manager, Finance Controller, Store Manager
Source: workflow W1249 — Consignment &amp; Vendor-Managed Inventory Shrinkage Monitoring &amp; Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1249_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1249_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1249_Lane2" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1249_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1249_Lane4" name="Inventory Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1249_Lane5" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1249_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1249_Start7" name="Scheduled — monthly consignment reconciliation cycle; ad-hoc triggered by consignment…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1249_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1249_Task8" name="Monthly consignment physical count">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly consignment physical count: At month-end, Store Manager coordinates with vendor representative to conduct joint physical count of all consignment goods: (a) count every consignment SKU on sales floor and in backroom; (b) compare to vendor&#x27;s consignment inventory record; (c) document variance by SKU (units over/short vs. vendor record); (d) identify damaged, defective, or display-worn consignment items requiring return to vendor
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Vendor Representative
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours per store per month (consignment section only)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1249_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1249_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1249_Task9" name="VMI sell-through reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VMI sell-through reconciliation: Monthly reconciliation of VMI vendor sell-through: (a) extract POS scan data for all VMI SKUs; (b) compare POS sell-through to vendor&#x27;s reported replenishment deliveries; (c) calculate implied on-hand: opening stock + deliveries – POS sales = implied on-hand; (d) flag any SKU where implied on-hand differs from physical count by &gt; 2%; (e) investigate variances as potential scanning fraud, unrecorded damage, or receiving discrepancies
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / Inventory Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1249_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1249_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1249_Task10" name="Consignment shrinkage allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Consignment shrinkage allocation: For confirmed consignment losses: (a) review consignment agreement for loss responsibility clause — typically: (i) theft/damage during display: shared loss (50/50) or vendor bears if within vendor-controlled display fixture, (ii) theft due to inadequate store security: BuildRight bears loss, (iii) force majeure (typhoon, flood): vendor bears loss or insurance claim; (b) calculate loss value at vendor&#x27;s consignment cost (not BuildRight SRP); (c) generate shrinkage allocation report with supporting documentation; (d) submit to vendor for acceptance or dispute
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1249_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1249_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1249_Task11" name="VMI replenishment discrepancy investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: VMI replenishment discrepancy investigation: When VMI replenishment quantity differs from expected: (a) compare vendor delivery docket to physical goods received; (b) verify VMI data feed accuracy — ensure POS sell-through data is being transmitted correctly to vendor system; (c) check for unreported in-store transfers or returns that were not captured in VMI data; (d) if vendor over-supplied (phantom replenishment), notify Procurement for vendor discussion
Responsible (R): Inventory Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours per discrepancy</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1249_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1249_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1249_Task12" name="Quarterly consignment/VMI shrinkage review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly consignment/VMI shrinkage review: LP Manager consolidates chain-wide consignment and VMI shrinkage results: (a) compare consignment shrinkage rate to owned-inventory shrinkage rate; (b) identify vendors with consistently high shrinkage rates (&gt; 2%); (c) review VMI data accuracy scorecard — on-time delivery fill rate, data feed error rate, stock-out frequency; (d) recommend vendors for consignment/VMI program continuation, modification, or conversion to standard purchase; (e) present findings to VP Merchandising and CFO
Responsible (R): LP Manager (Regional)
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1249_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1249_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1249_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1249_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1249_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-225 (ensure shrinkage detection &amp; case governance.) | - operational: LP Analyst / Inventory Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: LP Analyst / Inventory Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1249_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1249_Annotation14" targetRef="W1249_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
