    <bpmn:process id="W_W1336" name="W1336. Return Fraud &amp; Abuse Pattern Detection, Investigation &amp; Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Return exception alert from POS system (W12); LP Analyst identifies return fraud pattern during weekly exception review (W837); or Store Manager reports suspicious return activity
Frequency: Weekly pattern analysis; daily exception monitoring; ad-hoc investigation per detected pattern
Volume: ~56,000 returns/month across 200 stores (~2% of transactions per W1627); estimated 5–8% return fraud/abuse rate = ~2,800–4,500 fraudulent returns/month
Owner: LP Analyst
Participants: LP Manager (Regional), Store Manager, POS System Administrator, Finance Analyst, VP Legal (for prosecution cases)
Source: workflow W1336 — Return Fraud &amp; Abuse Pattern Detection, Investigation &amp; Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1336_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1336_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1336_Lane2" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1336_Lane3" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1336_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1336_Start5" name="Return exception alert from POS system (W12); LP Analyst identifies return fraud pattern…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1336_Task6" name="Automated return exception monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated return exception monitoring: POS system generates daily return exception alerts: (a) high-value returns (&gt; PHP 10,000) without receipt, (b) returns &gt; 3 by same customer within 30 days, (c) returns of items with high shoplifting risk per W1173 (power tools, electrical fittings), (d) returns processed by same cashier &gt; 5 per shift, (e) returns of items with activated serial numbers (power tools — indicates used item return), (f) returns at stores with return rate &gt; 5% of transactions (~2.5x the chain average); alerts routed to LP Analyst dashboard
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1336_Task7" name="Weekly return pattern analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly return pattern analysis: LP Analyst conducts weekly analysis of return data: (a) compile return exception report by store, cashier, customer (loyalty ID or tracked by ID), and SKU, (b) identify clusters: same customer returning at multiple stores, same cashier processing excessive exceptions, same SKU with disproportionate return rate, (c) cross-reference with shrinkage data per W845 — do high-return stores also have high shrinkage?, (d) cross-reference with CCTV review requests per W838 — correlate return timestamps with camera footage, (e) generate investigation list: top-10 suspicious patterns for the week
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager (Regional)
Duration: 4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1336_Task8" name="Investigation &amp; evidence gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Investigation &amp; evidence gathering: For each flagged pattern: (a) LP Analyst pulls transaction details: receipt images, POS logs, cashier ID, timestamp, items returned, tender refunded, (b) pulls CCTV footage from store per W838 for return timestamps — verify: did the customer bring the item? is the item condition consistent with return reason? (c) checks customer return history: how many returns in past 12 months? total value returned? which stores?, (d) checks cashier return history: does this cashier have disproportionate exception processing? cross-reference with employee access logs, (e) for switch fraud: compare returned item serial number/barcode to original sale record, (f) compile investigation file with evidence
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / LP Manager (Regional)
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1–3 days per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1336_Task9" name="Fraud confirmation &amp; response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fraud confirmation &amp; response: When fraud is confirmed: (a) Customer fraud: (i) flag customer in system — future returns require manager approval and photo ID, (ii) for PHP 10,000+ fraud: LP Manager coordinates with VP Legal for criminal complaint per W123 if warranted, (iii) for organized return fraud rings: coordinate with ORC investigation per W840, (b) Employee-collusion fraud: (i) initiate disciplinary process per W123, (ii) LP Manager interviews cashier with HR representative present per W123.5, (iii) administrative hearing and disciplinary action per DOLE requirements, (c) Process gap: if investigation reveals a policy or system gap enabling fraud (e.g., no receipt verification for items &gt; PHP 5,000), escalate to POS System Administrator and LP Manager for policy update
Responsible (R): LP Manager (Regional) / VP Legal
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: Per W123 investigation timeline</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1336_Task10" name="Prevention measures implementation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Prevention measures implementation: Based on investigation findings, implement prevention: (a) tighten return policy parameters in POS: (i) require manager key for returns &gt; PHP 5,000, (ii) require customer ID capture for returns without receipt (scan customer ID per RA 10173 compliance), (iii) enforce 30-day return window with system block for returns after policy period, (iv) serial number verification for power tools and electronics at return — scan serial number and match to original sale record, (b) cashier training: LP Training Coordinator includes return fraud detection in quarterly update per W846, (c) store signage: post return policy prominently at checkout and customer service desk, (d) vendor collaboration: for high-return categories (power tools), coordinate with vendor on tamper-evident packaging that shows evidence of opening
Responsible (R): LP Manager / POS System Administrator
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1–2 weeks per prevention measure</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1336_Task11" name="Monthly return fraud metrics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly return fraud metrics: LP Analyst compiles monthly return fraud dashboard: (a) return fraud cases detected, investigated, confirmed, (b) estimated fraud loss value (confirmed × average return value), (c) return exception rate by store — identify stores with improving or deteriorating rates, (d) prevention measure effectiveness: return fraud rate before and after prevention implementation, (e) employee-collusion cases as % of total return fraud, (f) report to National LP Director and VP Store Operations
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1336_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1336_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1336_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1336_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-312 (ensure controlled execution — Shrinkage Reduction (PA-23.3).) | - operational: risk-based approach (strict controls on high-risk items, lighter touch on low-risk); operational: defaulting to store credit for returns without receipt and manager approval for cash returns &gt; PHP 5,000; operational: quantity and weight verification at return for bulk items
Owner: LP Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1336_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1336_Annotation13" targetRef="W1336_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
