    <bpmn:process id="W_W1337" name="W1337. Organized Retail Crime (ORC) Intelligence Network, Case Management &amp; Law Enforcement Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: LP Analyst detects multi-store theft pattern during exception review (W837); ORC tip from law enforcement or industry intelligence sharing; or LP Manager identifies coordinated attack (multiple stores hit simultaneously)
Frequency: Ongoing intelligence monitoring; 5–10 active ORC cases at any time; quarterly law enforcement coordination meetings
Volume: Estimated 10–15 ORC groups operating in Philippine retail sector; BuildRight experiences ~20–30 ORC incidents/year (each involving 3+ stores)
Owner: National LP Director
Participants: LP Manager (Regional), LP Analyst, VP Legal, Law Enforcement (PNP, NBI), Industry ORC Intelligence Network, Store Manager
Source: workflow W1337 — Organized Retail Crime (ORC) Intelligence Network, Case Management &amp; Law Enforcement Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1337_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1337_Lane1" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1337_Lane2" name="National LP Director">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1337_Lane3" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1337_Lane4" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1337_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1337_Start6" name="LP Analyst detects multi-store theft pattern during exception review (W837); ORC tip from…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1337_Task7" name="Intelligence gathering &amp; network monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Intelligence gathering &amp; network monitoring: LP Analyst maintains ORC intelligence capability: (a) monitor online marketplaces (Shopee, Lazada, Facebook Marketplace, Carousell) for suspicious listings of BuildRight products at below-cost prices — indicates stolen merchandise resale, (b) participate in retail industry ORC intelligence sharing network (coordinate with SM Retail, Robinsons, Wilcon Depot through Philippine Retailers Association security committee), (c) monitor social media and local community groups for theft-related posts or suspicious bulk sales, (d) review incident reports from W837 and W840 for patterns suggesting ORC involvement: same vehicle at multiple stores, same individual using different disguises, coordinated timing across stores, (e) maintain ORC suspect database with photos, vehicle descriptions, known aliases, modus operandi
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1337_Task8" name="Case initiation &amp; profiling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Case initiation &amp; profiling: When ORC pattern detected: (a) LP Analyst opens ORC case file: case number, suspected group, stores affected, items targeted, estimated loss value, modus operandi, (b) compile evidence from all affected stores: CCTV per W838, POS transaction logs, exception reports per W837, employee witness statements, (c) create suspect profile: physical description, vehicle details (plate number, make, model), known associates, timing patterns (day of week, time of day), preferred store locations, (d) estimate total loss: aggregate losses across all incidents attributed to the group, (e) classify case severity: Major (estimated loss &gt; PHP 500,000 or 5+ stores affected), Standard (loss PHP 100,000–500,000, 2–4 stores)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / LP Manager
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 2–3 days per case initiation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1337_Task9" name="Law enforcement engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Law enforcement engagement: For Major cases: (a) National LP Director coordinates with PNP Criminal Investigation and Detection Group (CIDG) or NBI Anti-Organized Crime Division: (i) prepare case brief with evidence summary, loss value, suspect information, and jurisdiction (which cities/municipalities involved), (ii) submit formal complaint and request for investigation assistance, (iii) coordinate with VP Legal on legal strategy and evidence admissibility, (b) for Standard cases: LP Manager coordinates with local PNP station for each affected store location, (c) provide law enforcement with: CCTV footage (properly preserved per chain-of-custody requirements), incident reports, stolen merchandise descriptions with serial numbers, financial impact documentation
Responsible (R): National LP Director / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1337_Task10" name="Surveillance &amp; apprehension support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Surveillance &amp; apprehension support: When law enforcement conducts surveillance or entrapment operation: (a) LP Manager coordinates store-level support: staff awareness (without tipping off suspects), CCTV monitoring, safe communication channel with law enforcement, (b) ensure employee safety: apprehension is conducted by law enforcement, not BuildRight staff, (c) document apprehension: time, location, suspects, recovered merchandise, law enforcement officer names and badge numbers, (d) coordinate with VP Legal on criminal complaint filing and evidence preservation
Responsible (R): LP Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: Per operation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1337_Task11" name="Case prosecution support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Case prosecution support: After apprehension: (a) VP Legal coordinates with public prosecutor (fiscal) for case filing: prepare sworn statements from LP staff, CCTV evidence properly authenticated, merchandise recovery documentation, financial impact statement, (b) LP Analyst tracks case through criminal justice system: filing → arraignment → trial → resolution (Philippine criminal cases may take 1–3 years), (c) attend court hearings as witness when required, (d) maintain case file with all legal documents and court dates, (e) for cases resulting in conviction: document restitution order and coordinate with VP Legal for recovery
Responsible (R): VP Legal / LP Manager
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Ongoing per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1337_Task12" name="Quarterly ORC intelligence review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly ORC intelligence review: National LP Director convenes quarterly ORC intelligence review: (a) review all active ORC cases: status, new evidence, law enforcement progress, (b) update ORC suspect database with new intelligence, (c) share anonymized intelligence with industry ORC network, (d) review prevention effectiveness: are ORC groups targeting different stores or items after prevention measures implemented?, (e) brief COO and CEO on significant ORC activity trends
Responsible (R): National LP Director
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Half day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1337_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1337_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1337_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1337_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-312 (ensure controlled execution — Shrinkage Reduction (PA-23.3).) | - operational: building ongoing relationships and presenting well-documented cases; operational: limiting access to LP personnel, securing data, and purging records after case resolution; operational: reporting through platform fraud channels and working with DTI for enforcement
Owner: National LP Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1337_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1337_Annotation14" targetRef="W1337_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow16" sourceRef="W1337_Start6" targetRef="W1337_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow17" sourceRef="W1337_Task7" targetRef="W1337_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow18" sourceRef="W1337_Task8" targetRef="W1337_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow19" sourceRef="W1337_Task9" targetRef="W1337_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow20" sourceRef="W1337_Task10" targetRef="W1337_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow21" sourceRef="W1337_Task11" targetRef="W1337_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1337_Flow22" sourceRef="W1337_Task12" targetRef="W1337_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1337_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1337_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1337">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1337_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1337_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1337_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1337_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1337_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1337_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1337_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1337_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1337_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1337_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1337_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1337_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
