    <bpmn:process id="W_W1338" name="W1338. Employee Theft Prevention, Behavioral Analytics &amp; Internal Investigation Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Exception report anomaly suggesting internal theft (W837); cash variance pattern per cashier (W272); inventory shrinkage concentrated in specific departments or shifts (W845); anonymous tip per W79; or behavioral analytics alert
Frequency: Continuous behavioral monitoring; ~20–30 internal investigations per year; quarterly trend analysis
Volume: Internal theft estimated at 40–45% of total shrinkage in Philippine retail (~PHP 120–180M annually at BuildRight&#x27;s scale)
Owner: LP Manager (Regional)
Participants: LP Analyst, HR Manager, Store Manager, Head of Internal Audit, VP Legal, CHRO
Source: workflow W1338 — Employee Theft Prevention, Behavioral Analytics &amp; Internal Investigation Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1338_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1338_Lane1" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1338_Lane2" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1338_Lane3" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1338_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1338_Start5" name="Exception report anomaly suggesting internal theft (W837); cash variance pattern per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1338_Task6" name="Behavioral analytics &amp; exception monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Behavioral analytics &amp; exception monitoring: LP Analyst monitors employee behavior indicators: (a) POS exception reports per W837: cashier-specific void rate, refund rate, discount override rate, no-sale (drawer open) frequency — flag cashiers exceeding 2× the store average on any metric, (b) cash variance per cashier per W272: cumulative variance over 30 days (individual small variances may accumulate to significant losses), (c) receiving exceptions per W3: employees with higher-than-average receiving discrepancies in their departments, (d) time &amp; attendance anomalies: employees clocking in outside scheduled hours, buddy punching patterns (two employees alternating clock-in for each other), (e) lifestyle indicators (where observable): employee displaying purchasing behavior inconsistent with compensation level (reported by Store Manager, not investigated by LP directly — triggers investigation of POS activity), (f) system generates Employee Risk Score per cashier: weighted composite of exception metrics, updated weekly
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / System
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1338_Task7" name="Investigation trigger assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Investigation trigger assessment: When Employee Risk Score exceeds threshold or specific anomaly detected: (a) LP Analyst assesses whether anomaly has legitimate explanation (e.g., high void rate due to system errors, high refund rate due to legitimate customer returns during promotional period), (b) cross-reference with multiple data sources: POS exceptions + cash variances + receiving discrepancies — multiple indicators converging on same employee increases confidence, (c) review employee history: tenure, prior warnings, performance reviews, (d) if initial assessment suggests potential internal theft: escalate to LP Manager for formal investigation authorization
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours per assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1338_Task8" name="Covert investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Covert investigation: LP Manager conducts discreet investigation: (a) increase CCTV monitoring per W838 on suspected employee&#x27;s work area — focus on cash register, receiving dock, and stock room, (b) review all transactions by suspected employee for past 30 days: voids, refunds, discounts, no-sales, manual price overrides, (c) compare employee&#x27;s transaction patterns to peer group (other cashiers at same store during same period) — is the employee truly anomalous?, (d) for merchandise theft suspicions: conduct targeted spot inventory of items in employee&#x27;s work area — compare to system on-hand, (e) document all findings in investigation file with evidence preservation per W123 requirements, (f) investigation duration: 1–2 weeks (must be thorough but timely to limit ongoing losses)
Responsible (R): LP Manager / LP Analyst
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1338_Task9" name="Confrontation &amp; statement (if evidence sufficient)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Confrontation &amp; statement (if evidence sufficient): When investigation produces sufficient evidence: (a) LP Manager and HR Manager conduct formal interview with employee (two-on-one per DOLE best practice), (b) present evidence: transaction records, CCTV footage, inventory discrepancy data, (c) employee given opportunity to explain or respond to evidence, (d) document employee&#x27;s statement (written, signed by employee and both interviewers), (e) if employee admits: document admission with amount and method — this strengthens disciplinary case, (f) if employee denies despite evidence: proceed to administrative hearing based on documented evidence, (g) critical: ensure due process per DOLE requirements — failure to follow due process can result in illegal dismissal finding at NLRC even if employee was actually guilty
Responsible (R): LP Manager / HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO / VP Legal
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1338_Task10" name="Administrative hearing &amp; disciplinary action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Administrative hearing &amp; disciplinary action: (a) HR Manager issues Notice of Administrative Hearing per DOLE two-notice rule: (i) first notice: charges, evidence summary, hearing date (within 5 business days), (ii) hearing: employee may be represented by union representative or counsel, (iii) second notice: decision (within 5 business days of hearing), (b) disciplinary outcomes based on severity: (i) Minor (first offense, small amount &lt; PHP 5,000): written warning + restitution agreement, (ii) Moderate (PHP 5,000–50,000 or repeat offense): suspension (30 days maximum per DOLE) + restitution, (iii) Severe (&gt; PHP 50,000, ORC involvement, or vendor collusion): termination for just cause per Labor Code Article 297(a) — theft and serious misconduct, (c) for severe cases: VP Legal assesses criminal complaint per W123 — prepare evidence for PNP or NBI referral, (d) update LP case management system with outcome and lessons learned
Responsible (R): HR Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 weeks (two-notice process)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1338_Task11" name="Prevention reinforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Prevention reinforcement: After each resolved case: (a) LP Training Coordinator incorporates case study (anonymized) into LP training per W846, (b) LP Manager reviews with Store Manager: what controls failed? what prevention measures should be strengthened?, (c) update Employee Risk Score model if investigation revealed new behavioral indicators, (d) quarterly: LP Analyst compiles internal theft trend report: cases by type, amount recovered, prevention measure effectiveness
Responsible (R): LP Manager / LP Analyst
Accountable (A): National LP Director
Duration: 1–2 days per case + quarterly reporting</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1338_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1338_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1338_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1338_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-312 (ensure controlled execution — Shrinkage Reduction (PA-23.3).) | - operational: requiring multiple converging indicators before investigation and LP Manager assessment; operational: HR-led process with VP Legal oversight
Owner: LP Manager (Regional)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1338_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1338_Annotation13" targetRef="W1338_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1338_Flow15" sourceRef="W1338_Start5" targetRef="W1338_Task6" />
