    <bpmn:process id="W_W1528" name="W1528. Store-Level Construction Material High-Value Shrinkage Hotspot Monitoring &amp; Intervention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly shrinkage report showing category-level losses exceeding threshold; monthly LP hotspot review
Frequency: Weekly monitoring dashboards; monthly intervention reviews; quarterly trend analysis
Volume: Target categories: power tools, electrical wire/cable, plumbing fixtures, tiles, paint (premium), and door hardware — representing ~15% of SKUs but ~40% of shrinkage value
Owner: LP Supervisor
Participants: LP Supervisor, Store Manager, LP Agents, Category Managers, POS Data Analyst
Source: workflow W1528 — Store-Level Construction Material High-Value Shrinkage Hotspot Monitoring &amp; Intervention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1528_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1528_Lane1" name="POS Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1528_Lane2" name="LP Agent">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1528_Lane3" name="LP Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1528_Lane4" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1528_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1528_Start6" name="Weekly shrinkage report showing category-level losses exceeding threshold; monthly LP…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1528_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1528_Task7" name="Weekly hotspot dashboard review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly hotspot dashboard review: (a) POS Data Analyst generates weekly shrinkage hotspot report per store: (i) sales vs. perpetual inventory variance by category (target categories: power tools, electrical, plumbing, premium paint, door hardware), (ii) top 20 SKUs with highest negative variance (units sold per POS vs. units expected from perpetual), (iii) zero-sales SKUs with inventory reduction (possible unrecorded loss), (iv) high-return-rate SKUs (potential return fraud — buy with receipt, return stolen unit); (b) LP Supervisor reviews dashboard; flags stores where any target category shrinkage exceeds PHP 5,000/week threshold
Responsible (R): POS Data Analyst / LP Supervisor
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1528_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1528_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1528_Task8" name="Hotspot area CCTV audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Hotspot area CCTV audit: (a) for flagged stores: LP Supervisor or LP Agent reviews CCTV footage for the hotspot category area during the reporting week; (b) looks for: (i) professional shoplifting patterns (group of 2–3 entering, one distracts, one conceals), (ii) customer spending unusual time in aisle without making purchase, (iii) customers entering store empty-handed and exiting with bulging bags/bulky items without POS receipt, (iv) employees in restricted areas outside normal duties; (c) documents findings with timestamped screenshots/video clips
Responsible (R): LP Agent / LP Supervisor
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/week per flagged store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1528_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1528_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1528_Task9" name="Merchandising security intervention">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merchandising security intervention: (a) based on hotspot analysis, LP Supervisor and Store Manager implement targeted interventions by category: (i) power tools: move high-value tools (PHP 5,000+) to locked display cabinet; customer requests tool → staff retrieves → escorts to POS; install alpha security cable devices on mid-range tools (PHP 2,000–5,000); (ii) electrical wire/cable: install pre-cut display samples only (no access to full rolls); customer selects gauge → staff cuts from secured backstock; (iii) plumbing fixtures: spider wrap on high-value faucets/showerheads; peg-hook security caps on smaller fittings; (iv) premium paint: security tag on premium gallons; quantity display limited to 3–4 units on shelf (backstock in locked cage); (v) door hardware: locked display for locksets &gt; PHP 2,000; (b) LP Supervisor tracks intervention compliance per store (photo evidence of locked displays, security devices installed)
Responsible (R): LP Supervisor / Store Manager
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours per store (initial setup)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1528_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1528_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1528_Task10" name="Monthly shrinkage review and trend analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly shrinkage review and trend analysis: (a) LP Supervisor compiles monthly shrinkage report for hotspot categories: (i) shrinkage value by category by store, (ii) before/after comparison (post-intervention vs. pre-intervention), (iii) shrinkage rate trend (target: reduce from 1.5% to 1.0% within 12 months), (iv) top 10 stores by shrinkage (for targeted intervention), (v) intervention compliance score by store; (b) presents to LP Manager, Category Managers, and VP Store Operations; (c) Category Managers review merchandising impact: (i) did locked displays reduce sell-through (sales impact), (ii) customer complaints about service delays (waiting for staff to unlock displays), (iii) is the shrinkage reduction worth the sales friction?
Responsible (R): LP Supervisor / Category Managers
Accountable (A): LP Manager / VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1528_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1528_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1528_Task11" name="Quarterly strategy adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly strategy adjustment: (a) LP Manager reviews quarterly results: (i) which interventions are effective (significant shrinkage reduction without sales impact), (ii) which need adjustment (too much sales friction or insufficient shrinkage reduction), (iii) emerging hotspot categories (e.g., seasonal items, new product launches); (b) adjusts strategy: (i) expand effective interventions to all 200 stores, (ii) modify or replace ineffective interventions, (iii) allocate LP capital budget for new security devices; (c) coordinates with W1337 (ORC) for external theft patterns and W1338 (Employee Theft) for internal patterns identified through hotspot analysis
Responsible (R): LP Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1528_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1528_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1528_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1528_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1528_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-312 (ensure controlled execution — Shrinkage Reduction (PA-23.3).) | - operational: LP Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: LP Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1528_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1528_Annotation13" targetRef="W1528_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
